  "result": {
    "text": "def sort_array(arr):\n    return sorted(arr, key=lambda x: (not bin(x).count('1'))), \n                sortby=lambda x: x)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import doctest\n    doctest.testmod()\n\n# The `sorted` function is here used with a custom key as the key.\n# The key is first the number of the ones in the binary representation. \n# The second key value is the number the same as the first key.\n\n\n\nThis implementation uses the Python-in `bin.count` function to count the number of ones in the binary representation. The `sorted` function is used with the number of ones as the first key.",
